-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, "Offences affecting life" and "Hurt":
-- the ten sections that pass 1 (2026-09-26) deferred for time, encoded in the
-- completion pass of 2026-11-04, by one Sonnet 5.5 agent.
--
-- Covers: s 301 (the description of a transferred culpable homicide), s 304B and
-- s 304C (deaths of a child, a domestic worker or a vulnerable person), s 308A
-- (death in furtherance of a group's object), ss 310 and 311 (infanticide),
-- s 314 (death caused by an act done with intent to cause miscarriage), s 315
-- (child destruction), s 316 (death of a quick unborn child) and s 335A
-- (allowing neglect, hurt or abuse of a domestic worker or vulnerable person).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO "Current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026" (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text),
-- registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt, sha256 066301837e6413cf...).
-- Each quotation below is a `-- src:N | text` line copied from that file by
-- generators/deferred/expand.py; each `@ref` carries the locator of its lines;
-- `python3 -I srcrefs.py check --refs <raw> <this file>` reports 0 problems.
--
-- What a reader must know before reading:
--
-- * The four items of the charge generator's contract (a facts record, a defining
--   predicate, `offence under s N`, `charge under s N`) are here for every
--   punishing provision, every one `@export`ed with `@desc`. A provision that
--   only defines (s 301, s 310) has no charge items of its own: s 301's culpable
--   homicide is punished under ss 302 and 304, and s 310's infanticide under s 311.
-- * Offence ladders are BOOLEAN by contract (notes/PLAN.md section 3): an
--   unstated element reaches them as FALSE, so a FALSE from a ladder means "the
--   elements are not made out on the facts stated", not "the Code says no".
--   The functions that DO carry the 2026-10-29 rule are the decision functions
--   that answer a MAYBE or a named constructor: they answer JUST FALSE or a
--   constructor of "the text says no" only where the text says no in its own
--   words, each such branch carrying a `-- FALSE-kind` comment, and answer
--   NOTHING with a `-- NOTHING-kind` comment where it does not. See
--   NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".
-- * "domestic worker" (s 73(4)), "vulnerable person" (s 74A(5)), "group" (the
--   Organised Crime Act 2015 s 2(1)), "sexual abuse" (the Criminal Procedure
--   Code 2010 s 2(1)) and the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974 are not defined in
--   this module's sources or belong to the general-part group: each rides as a
--   BOOLEAN leaf whose @desc names its owner (notes/PLAN.md section 1). The
--   drill-downs for ss 73(4) and 74A(5) are `domestic worker within section 73`
--   and `vulnerable person within section 74A` in pc-general-part.l4.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-body-a-life`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, the sections deferred in pass 1 (ss 301-335A)`

§§ `s 301 - culpable homicide by causing the death of a person other than the person whose death was intended`

-- src:6793 | Culpable homicide by causing the death of a person other than the person whose
-- src:6794 | death was intended
-- src:6796 | 301.—(1) If a person, by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to
-- src:6797 | cause death, commits culpable homicide by causing the death of any person whose death
-- src:6798 | he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause, the culpable homicide
-- src:6799 | committed by the offender is of the description of which it would have been if he had
-- src:6800 | caused the death of the person whose death he intended or knew himself to be likely to
-- src:6801 | cause.
-- src:6805 | (2) To avoid doubt, in the circumstances mentioned in subsection (1), the accused
-- src:6806 | person may rely on any defence or exception in law as though the accused person had
-- src:6807 | caused the death of the person whose death he intended or knew himself to be likely to
-- src:6808 | cause.
-- Subsection (2) is encoded in pc-exceptions.l4 (`the accused person may rely on a
-- defence under section 301(2)`, over `Transferred Defence Facts`), which pass 1
-- wrote under PLAN section 5; it is not written twice. Subsection (1) is here.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 301(1) (src:6793-6808)
DECLARE `Description of culpable homicide` IS ONE OF
    `of the description of murder`
    `of the description of culpable homicide not amounting to murder`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 301(1) (src:6796-6801)
@export The description of the culpable homicide the accused committed when he caused the death of a person other than the one whose death he intended or knew likely (s 301(1) of the Penal Code 1871): the description it would have had if he had caused the intended person's death; NOTHING where the section does not say
GIVEN intended IS A `Homicide Facts` @desc The accused's act and state of mind, stated as if he had caused the death of the person whose death he intended or knew himself to be likely to cause - with every Exception to section 300 that would then apply
      circumstances IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these the circumstances of s 301(1): by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to cause death, the accused commits culpable homicide by causing the death of a person whose death he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Description of culpable homicide`
`s 301(1) the description of the culpable homicide` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (circumstances)
        THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 301(1) speaks only of a person who, "by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to cause death, commits culpable homicide by causing the death of any person whose death he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause"
        IF `commits murder` intended
        THEN JUST `of the description of murder`
        IF `commits culpable homicide not amounting to murder` intended
        THEN JUST `of the description of culpable homicide not amounting to murder`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section gives a description only by comparison with culpable homicide of the intended person; where the facts stated as if that person had died are not culpable homicide, it names none

§§ `ss 310 and 311 - infanticide`

-- src:7179 | Infanticide
-- src:7181 | 310. When any woman by any intentional act or omission causes the death of her
-- src:7182 | child being a child below 12 months of age, but at the time of the act or omission the
-- src:7183 | balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the
-- src:7184 | effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon
-- src:7185 | the birth of the child, she shall, notwithstanding that the circumstances were such that but
-- src:7186 | for this section the offence would have amounted to murder, be guilty of the offence of
-- src:7187 | infanticide.
-- src:7191 | Punishment for infanticide
-- src:7193 | 311. Whoever commits the offence of infanticide shall be punished at the discretion
-- src:7194 | of the court with imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:7195 | extend to 10 years, and shall, if she is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be
-- src:7196 | liable to fine.
-- 310 does not make the killing an element ("notwithstanding that ... the offence
-- would have amounted to murder"): it removes the bar of murder, so the ladder
-- asks for the woman, the intentional act or omission, her child under 12
-- months, and the disturbance of the balance of her mind (FORK DEF-A1).
@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 310, 311 (src:7179-7196)
DECLARE `Infanticide Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes the child, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did or omitted to do, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by smothering the said child"
    `the accused is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused a woman - a female human being of any age (s 10)?
    `by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, by an intentional act or omission (s 26C), cause the death of her child?
    `the child is below 12 months of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the child below 12 months of age? Set from the helper `below 12 months of age` on the child's age in months (pc-body-a-life.l4)
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, was the balance of her mind disturbed because she had not fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child?
    `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, was the balance of her mind disturbed by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth of the child?

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 310 (src:7181-7187)
@export Whether the accused commits "the offence of infanticide" within section 310 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Infanticide Facts` @desc The woman, her act or omission, the child, and the balance of her mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits infanticide within section 310` f IF
        "When any woman"
   ...  f's `the accused is a woman`
   ...  f's `by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child`
   ...  "being a child below 12 months of age"
   ...  f's `the child is below 12 months of age`
   ...  "but at the time of the act or omission the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of"
   ...  (    f's `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child`
        OR   f's `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth of the child` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 311 (src:7193-7196)
`punishment prescribed by s 311` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "311"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall, if she is not sentenced to imprisonment for life, also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 311 (src:7193-7196)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 311 of the Penal Code 1871 (infanticide)
GIVEN f IS A `Infanticide Facts` @desc The woman, her act or omission, the child, and the balance of her mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 311` f IF
        "Whoever commits the offence of infanticide"
   ...  `commits infanticide within section 310` f

GIVEN f IS A `Infanticide Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of infanticide not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is a woman`) "the accused is a woman"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child`) "by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the child is below 12 months of age`) "the child is below 12 months of age"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child` OR f's `the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth of the child`) "at the time the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth, or by the effect of lactation"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits infanticide within section 310` f) "the elements of section 310 taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 311 (src:7193-7196)
@export Frame a charge under section 311 of the Penal Code 1871 (infanticide), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Infanticide Facts` @desc The woman, her act or omission, the child, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 311` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "311" "infanticide"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 311`'s words)
        (`offence under s 311` f)
        (CONCAT "did, being a woman, by an intentional act or omission cause the death of her child, ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", a child below 12 months of age, at a time when the balance of your mind was disturbed by reason of the effect of giving birth to the said child or of lactation, and thereby commit the offence of infanticide, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of infanticide not made out` f)


§§ `s 304B - causing death of child below 14 years of age, domestic worker or vulnerable person by sustained abuse`

-- src:6859 | Causing death of child below 14 years of age, domestic worker or vulnerable person
-- src:6860 | by sustained abuse
-- src:6862 | 304B.—(1) A relevant person who causes the death of any child, domestic worker or
-- src:6863 | vulnerable person by sustained abuse shall be punished with —
-- src:6865 | (a) imprisonment for life and shall also be liable to caning; or
-- src:6867 | (b) imprisonment for a term which may extend to 30 years, and shall also be
-- src:6868 | liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:6872 | (2) In this section —
-- src:6874 | “child” means a person below 14 years of age;
-- src:6876 | “domestic worker”, “employer”, “employment agent” and “member of the
-- src:6879 | employer’s household” have the meanings given by section 73(4);
-- src:6881 | “neglect” means the failure by a relevant person to provide any or adequate
-- src:6882 | essential care (such as but not limited to food, clothing, medical aid, lodging
-- src:6883 | and other necessities of life) to the extent of causing personal injury or physical
-- src:6884 | pain to, or injury to the physical health of any child, domestic worker or
-- src:6885 | vulnerable person;
-- src:6887 | “relevant person” means —
-- src:6889 | (a) in the case of a child, a person who has custody, charge or care of the
-- src:6890 | child;
-- src:6892 | (b) in the case of a domestic worker, the employer of the domestic
-- src:6893 | worker, a member of the employer’s household or the employment
-- src:6894 | agent of the domestic worker; and
-- src:6896 | (c) in the case of a vulnerable person, a person who has custody, charge
-- src:6897 | or care of the vulnerable person;
-- src:6899 | “sustained abuse” means a course of conduct which consists of voluntarily causing
-- src:6900 | hurt or knowingly causing neglect, or both, of a child, domestic worker or
-- src:6901 | vulnerable person on —
-- src:6903 | (a) 2 or more occasions; or
-- src:6905 | (b) a single occasion if the conduct is protracted;
-- src:6907 | “vulnerable person” has the meaning given by section 74A(5).
-- (1)(a) and (1)(b) are the two punishments the section offers; the text does not
-- say when the court gives which, so the one record carries both (as s 304(a)
-- carries its (i) and (ii)), and the charge states the words (FORK DEF-A2).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B (src:6859-6907)
DECLARE `Sustained Abuse Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person who died, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did or caused, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by repeatedly striking the said child and withholding food"
    `the victim is a child below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died below 14 years of age (s 304B(2) "child")? Set from the helper `s 304B(2) the person is a child` on the age in years
    `the victim is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died a "domestic worker" as section 73(4) gives the meaning? That definition is the general-part group's: see `domestic worker within section 73` in pc-general-part.l4
    `the victim is a vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died a "vulnerable person" as section 74A(5) gives the meaning? That definition is the general-part group's: see `vulnerable person within section 74A` in pc-general-part.l4
    `the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused have the custody, charge or care of the person who died? (s 304B(2) "relevant person", paragraphs (a) and (c))
    `the accused is the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household, or the domestic worker's employment agent (as s 73(4) gives those meanings)? (s 304B(2) "relevant person", paragraph (b))
    `the conduct consists of voluntarily causing hurt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course of conduct consist, in whole or in part, of voluntarily causing hurt (s 321) to the person who died?
    `the conduct consists of knowingly causing neglect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the course of conduct consist, in whole or in part, of knowingly causing neglect to the person who died? "Neglect" is `neglect within section 304B(2)`
    `the conduct took place on 2 or more occasions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the conduct take place on 2 or more occasions? Set from the helper `2 or more occasions` on the number of occasions (s 304B(2) "sustained abuse", paragraph (a))
    `the conduct took place on a single occasion and was protracted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the conduct take place on a single occasion and was it protracted? (s 304B(2) "sustained abuse", paragraph (b)) Whether conduct is "protracted" is the court's judgement: the text does not define it
    `causes the death of the victim by the course of conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused cause the death of the person who died by that course of conduct? (s 304B(1) "causes the death ... by sustained abuse")

DECLARE `Neglect Facts` HAS
    `fails to provide any or adequate essential care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the relevant person fail to provide any, or adequate, essential care (such as but not limited to food, clothing, medical aid, lodging and other necessities of life)?
    `to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain, or injury to physical health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain to, or injury to the physical health of, the child, domestic worker or vulnerable person?

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(2) "child" (src:6874-6874)
@export Whether a person of the given age is a "child" within section 304B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 ("a person below 14 years of age"); the text says no to anyone of 14 or over
GIVEN years IS A NUMBER @desc The person's age in completed years
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304B(2) the person is a child` MEANS
    IF `below 14 years of age` years
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"child\" means a person below 14 years of age"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(2) "sustained abuse" paragraph (a) (src:6903-6903)
@export Whether a number of occasions is "2 or more occasions" (s 304B(2) "sustained abuse", paragraph (a), of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN occasions IS A NUMBER @desc On how many occasions the conduct took place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2 or more occasions` occasions IF occasions AT LEAST 2

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(2) "neglect" (src:6881-6885)
@export Whether a failure to provide care is "neglect" within section 304B(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (also used by section 335A(6))
GIVEN n IS A `Neglect Facts` @desc The failure to provide essential care, and its effect
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304B(2) the failure is neglect` MEANS
    IF n's `fails to provide any or adequate essential care` AND n's `to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain, or injury to physical health`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"neglect\" means the failure by a relevant person to provide any or adequate essential care ... to the extent of causing personal injury or physical pain to, or injury to the physical health of ..."

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(2) "relevant person" (src:6887-6897)
@export Whether the accused is a "relevant person" within section 304B(2) of the Penal Code 1871, by the kind of person who died
GIVEN f IS A `Sustained Abuse Facts` @desc Who died, and the accused's relation to them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `relevant person within section 304B(2)` f IF
        (        "(a) in the case of a child, a person who has custody, charge or care of the child"
            ...  f's `the victim is a child below 14 years of age`
            ...  f's `the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim` )
    OR  (        "(b) in the case of a domestic worker, the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker"
            ...  f's `the victim is a domestic worker`
            ...  f's `the accused is the employer of the domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker` )
    OR  (        "(c) in the case of a vulnerable person, a person who has custody, charge or care of the vulnerable person"
            ...  f's `the victim is a vulnerable person`
            ...  f's `the accused has custody, charge or care of the victim` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(2) "sustained abuse" (src:6899-6905)
@export Whether the conduct is "sustained abuse" within section 304B(2) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Sustained Abuse Facts` @desc The course of conduct and how often it took place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` f IF
        "a course of conduct which consists of voluntarily causing hurt or knowingly causing neglect, or both"
   ...  (    f's `the conduct consists of voluntarily causing hurt`
        OR   f's `the conduct consists of knowingly causing neglect` )
   ...  "of a child, domestic worker or vulnerable person on"
   ...  (    f's `the conduct took place on 2 or more occasions`
        OR   f's `the conduct took place on a single occasion and was protracted` )

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(1) (src:6862-6868)
@export Whether the accused "causes the death of any child, domestic worker or vulnerable person by sustained abuse" within section 304B(1) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Sustained Abuse Facts` @desc Who died, the accused's relation to them, and the course of conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `causes death by sustained abuse within section 304B(1)` f IF
        "A relevant person"
   ...  `relevant person within section 304B(2)` f
   ...  "who causes the death of any child, domestic worker or vulnerable person by sustained abuse"
   ...  (    f's `the victim is a child below 14 years of age`
        OR   f's `the victim is a domestic worker`
        OR   f's `the victim is a vulnerable person` )
   ...  `sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` f
   ...  f's `causes the death of the victim by the course of conduct`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(1) (src:6862-6868)
`punishment prescribed by s 304B(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "304B(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life and shall also be liable to caning; or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 30 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 360
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(1) (src:6862-6868)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 304B(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing death by sustained abuse)
GIVEN f IS A `Sustained Abuse Facts` @desc Who died, the accused's relation to them, and the course of conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 304B(1)` f IF
        "shall be punished with"
   ...  `causes death by sustained abuse within section 304B(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Sustained Abuse Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of causing death by sustained abuse not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the victim is a child below 14 years of age` OR f's `the victim is a domestic worker` OR f's `the victim is a vulnerable person`) "the person who died is a child below 14 years of age, a domestic worker or a vulnerable person"),
        (`missing unless` (`relevant person within section 304B(2)` f) "the accused is a relevant person: has custody, charge or care of the child or vulnerable person, or is the employer, a member of the employer's household or the employment agent of the domestic worker"),
        (`missing unless` (`sustained abuse within section 304B(2)` f) "a course of conduct of voluntarily causing hurt or knowingly causing neglect, or both, on 2 or more occasions or on a single occasion if the conduct is protracted"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `causes the death of the victim by the course of conduct`) "the accused causes the death by that course of conduct"),
        (`missing unless` (`causes death by sustained abuse within section 304B(1)` f) "the elements of section 304B(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304B(1) (src:6862-6868)
@export Frame a charge under section 304B(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing death of child, domestic worker or vulnerable person by sustained abuse), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Sustained Abuse Facts` @desc Who died, the course of conduct, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 304B(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "304B(1)" "causing death of child below 14 years of age, domestic worker or vulnerable person by sustained abuse"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 304B(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 304B(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being a relevant person, did cause the death of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), ", ",
                (IF f's `the victim is a child below 14 years of age` THEN "a child below 14 years of age" ELSE IF f's `the victim is a domestic worker` THEN "a domestic worker" ELSE "a vulnerable person"),
                ", by sustained abuse, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of causing death by sustained abuse not made out` f)


§§ `s 304C - causing or allowing death of child below 14 years of age, domestic worker or vulnerable person in same household`

-- src:6911 | Causing or allowing death of child below 14 years of age, domestic worker or
-- src:6912 | vulnerable person in same household
-- src:6914 | 304C.—(1) A person (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:6916 | (a) a person below 14 years of age, a domestic worker or a vulnerable person
-- src:6917 | (B) dies as a result of the unlawful act of a person who —
-- src:6918 | (i) was a member of the same household as B; and
-- src:6920 | (ii) had frequent contact with B;
-- src:6922 | (b) A was a member of the same household as B, and had frequent contact with
-- src:6923 | B at the time of that act;
-- src:6925 | (c) at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B
-- src:6928 | by the unlawful act of such a person; and
-- src:6930 | (d) either A was the person whose act caused B’s death or —
-- src:6931 | (i) A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk
-- src:6932 | mentioned in paragraph (c);
-- src:6934 | (ii) A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been
-- src:6935 | expected to take to protect B from the significant risk; and
-- src:6937 | (iii) the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A
-- src:6938 | foresaw or ought to have foreseen.
-- src:6942 | (2) The prosecution does not have to prove whether it is the first alternative element
-- src:6943 | in subsection (1)(d) or the second alternative element (sub-paragraphs (i), (ii) and (iii) of
-- src:6944 | subsection (1)(d)) that applies.
-- src:6948 | (3) A is not guilty of an offence under this section if A could not have been expected
-- src:6949 | in A’s circumstances to take any such step as is mentioned in subsection (1)(d)(ii).
-- src:6953 | (4) Any person who is guilty of an offence under this section shall be punished with
-- src:6956 | (a) imprisonment for life and shall also be liable to caning; or
-- src:6958 | (b) imprisonment for a term which may extend to 30 years, and shall also be
-- src:6959 | liable to fine or to caning.
-- src:6963 | (5) For the purposes of this section —
-- src:6965 | (a) a person is to be regarded as a “member” of a particular household, even if
-- src:6966 | that person does not live in that household, if that person visits it so often
-- src:6967 | and for such periods of time that it is reasonable to regard him as a member
-- src:6968 | of the particular household;
-- src:6970 | (b) where B lived in different households at different times, “the same
-- src:6971 | household as B” refers to the household in which B was living at the time
-- src:6972 | of the act that caused B’s death;
-- src:6974 | (c) an “unlawful” act, other than an act by A, is one that constitutes an offence
-- src:6975 | or would constitute an offence but for being the act of —
-- src:6976 | (i) a person below the age specified in section 82;
-- src:6979 | (ii) a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained
-- src:6980 | sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and
-- src:6981 | consequence of the act;
-- src:6983 | (iii) a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind;
-- src:6985 | (iv) a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication; or
-- src:6987 | (v) a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact;
-- src:6989 | (d) “domestic worker” and “vulnerable person” have the meanings given by
-- src:6990 | sections 73(4) and 74A(5), respectively; and
-- src:6992 | (e) the circumstances mentioned in subsection (3) include but is not limited to
-- src:6993 | A’s past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt,
-- src:6994 | sexual abuse or any injury to A’s mental health as a result of an unlawful
-- src:6995 | act by any member of the same household as A.
-- Subsection (2) says the prosecution need not prove WHICH alternative of (1)(d)
-- applies; the ladder is the OR of the two, which is exactly that (FORK DEF-A3).
-- Subsection (3) reads as a flat negative for the whole offence; the other reading,
-- that it only answers the second alternative, is registered as FORK DEF-A4.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C (src:6911-6995)
DECLARE `Household Death Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person who died (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What was done or not done, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by failing to protect the said child from repeated assaults by another member of the household"
    `B is below 14 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died (B) below 14 years of age? Set from the helper `below 14 years of age` on B's age
    `B is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was B a "domestic worker" as section 73(4) gives the meaning (s 304C(5)(d))? See `domestic worker within section 73` in pc-general-part.l4
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was B a "vulnerable person" as section 74A(5) gives the meaning (s 304C(5)(d))? See `vulnerable person within section 74A` in pc-general-part.l4
    `B dies as a result of an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did B die as a result of an unlawful act of a person (s 304C(1)(a))? An act is "unlawful" as `s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` says
    `the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person whose unlawful act it was a member of the same household as B (s 304C(1)(a)(i))? "Member" and "the same household" are read with s 304C(5)(a) and (b)
    `the person who did that act had frequent contact with B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person whose unlawful act it was have frequent contact with B (s 304C(1)(a)(ii))? The text does not define "frequent"
    `A was a member of the same household as B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused (A) a member of the same household as B at the time of that act (s 304C(1)(b))? Read with s 304C(5)(a) and (b)
    `A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A have frequent contact with B at the time of that act (s 304C(1)(b))?
    `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At that time was there a significant risk of grievous hurt (s 320) being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person (s 304C(1)(c))? The text does not define "significant"
    `A was the person whose act caused B's death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was A the person whose act caused B's death (s 304C(1)(d), first alternative)?
    `A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was A, or ought A to have been, aware of the significant risk (s 304C(1)(d)(i))?
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A fail to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk (s 304C(1)(d)(ii))?
    `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the unlawful act occur in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen (s 304C(1)(d)(iii))?
    `A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could A not have been expected, in A's circumstances, to take any such step as s 304C(1)(d)(ii) mentions (s 304C(3))? A's circumstances include but are not limited to A's past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to A's mental health as a result of an unlawful act by any member of the same household as A (s 304C(5)(e)); answer FALSE unless that is shown

DECLARE `Unlawful Act Facts` HAS
    `the act is an act of A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an act of the accused (A) himself or herself? The definition below speaks only of acts "other than an act by A"
    `the act constitutes an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act constitute an offence? (for s 335A(3), an offence that causes neglect, hurt, grievous hurt or sexual abuse to B or injury to B's mental health)
    `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person below the age specified in section 82` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act constitute an offence but for being the act of a person below the age specified in section 82?
    `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act constitute an offence but for being the act of a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of the act?
    `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind (s 84)?
    `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication (s 85)?
    `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the act constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact (s 79)?

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(5)(c) (src:6974-6987)
@export Whether an act other than an act by the accused is "unlawful" within section 304C(5)(c) of the Penal Code 1871: an offence, or one that would be but for the actor's age, immaturity, unsoundness of mind, intoxication or mistake of fact
GIVEN u IS A `Unlawful Act Facts` @desc The act, and whether it is an offence or would be but for the actor's excuse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304C(5)(c) the act is unlawful` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF u's `the act is an act of A`
        THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the definition covers an "unlawful" act "other than an act by A"; what makes A's own act unlawful the section does not say
        IF u's `the act constitutes an offence`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person below the age specified in section 82`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of the act`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an \"unlawful\" act, other than an act by A, is one that constitutes an offence or would constitute an offence but for being the act of ..." (FORK DEF-A5: a definition read as closed)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(5)(a) (src:6965-6968)
@export Whether a person who does not live in a household is to be regarded as a "member" of it within section 304C(5)(a) of the Penal Code 1871: he visits it so often and for such periods of time that it is reasonable to regard him as a member
GIVEN `visits so often and for such periods that it is reasonable to regard him as a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person visit the household so often, and for such periods of time, that it is reasonable to regard him as a member of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304C(5)(a) the person who does not live in the household is a member of it` MEANS
    IF `visits so often and for such periods that it is reasonable to regard him as a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only adds to those who are members ("is to be regarded as a 'member' ... even if that person does not live in that household, if ..."); it does not say that a person who does not visit so often is not a member

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(5)(b) (src:6970-6972)
@export Whether the household A belongs to is "the same household as B" within section 304C(5)(b) of the Penal Code 1871: where B lived in different households at different times, the household in which B was living at the time of the act that caused B's death
GIVEN `the household in which B was living at the time of the act that caused B's death` IS A STRING @desc The household in which B was living at the time of that act, as the charge is to name it
      `the household of which A is a member` IS A STRING @desc The household of which A is a member at the time of that act, named the same way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304C(5)(b) the household is the same household as B` MEANS
    IF `the household in which B was living at the time of the act that caused B's death` EQUALS `the household of which A is a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where B lived in different households at different times, 'the same household as B' refers to the household in which B was living at the time of the act that caused B's death" - any other household of B's is not the one

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(5)(e) (src:6992-6995)
@export Whether an experience is among "A's circumstances" under section 304C(5)(e) of the Penal Code 1871 (A's past or present suffering of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health at the hands of a member of A's household)
GIVEN `A has past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to A's mental health as a result of an unlawful act by a member of the same household as A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A have such experiences?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304C(5)(e) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` MEANS
    IF `A has past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to A's mental health as a result of an unlawful act by a member of the same household as A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): A's circumstances "include but is not limited to" those experiences, so any other circumstance may count

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(1) (src:6914-6938)
@export Whether the accused (A) commits the offence in section 304C(1) of the Penal Code 1871: a death in the same household, with A's own act or A's failure to protect
GIVEN f IS A `Household Death Facts` @desc B, the household, the unlawful act, the risk, and what A did or failed to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of causing or allowing death in the same household within section 304C(1)` f IF
        "a person below 14 years of age, a domestic worker or a vulnerable person (B)"
   ...  (    f's `B is below 14 years of age`
        OR   f's `B is a domestic worker`
        OR   f's `B is a vulnerable person` )
   ...  "(a) dies as a result of the unlawful act of a person who was a member of the same household as B and had frequent contact with B"
   ...  f's `B dies as a result of an unlawful act`
   ...  f's `the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B`
   ...  f's `the person who did that act had frequent contact with B`
   ...  "(b) A was a member of the same household as B, and had frequent contact with B at the time of that act"
   ...  f's `A was a member of the same household as B`
   ...  f's `A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act`
   ...  "(c) at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person"
   ...  f's `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person`
   ...  "(d) either A was the person whose act caused B's death or"
   ...  (    f's `A was the person whose act caused B's death`
        OR   (        f's `A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk`
                 ...  f's `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk`
                 ...  f's `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` ) )
   ...  "(3) A is not guilty of an offence under this section if A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step"
   ...  NOT (f's `A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A is not guilty of an offence under this section if A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step as is mentioned in subsection (1)(d)(ii)"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(4) (src:6953-6959)
`punishment prescribed by s 304C(4)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "304C(4)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life and shall also be liable to caning; or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 30 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 360
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(4) (src:6953-6959)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 304C(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing or allowing death of child, domestic worker or vulnerable person in same household)
GIVEN f IS A `Household Death Facts` @desc B, the household, the unlawful act, the risk, and what A did or failed to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 304C(4)` f IF
        "Any person who is guilty of an offence under this section"
   ...  `commits the offence of causing or allowing death in the same household within section 304C(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Household Death Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of causing or allowing death in the same household not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is below 14 years of age` OR f's `B is a domestic worker` OR f's `B is a vulnerable person`) "B is a person below 14 years of age, a domestic worker or a vulnerable person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B dies as a result of an unlawful act` AND f's `the person who did that act was a member of the same household as B` AND f's `the person who did that act had frequent contact with B`) "B dies as a result of the unlawful act of a person who was a member of the same household as B and had frequent contact with B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A was a member of the same household as B` AND f's `A had frequent contact with B at the time of that act`) "A was a member of the same household as B, and had frequent contact with B at the time of that act"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person`) "at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to B by the unlawful act of such a person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A was the person whose act caused B's death` OR (f's `A was, or ought to have been, aware of the significant risk` AND f's `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take to protect B from the significant risk` AND f's `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen`)) "either A was the person whose act caused B's death, or A was or ought to have been aware of the significant risk, failed to take the steps A could reasonably have been expected to take, and the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind A foresaw or ought to have foreseen"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `A could not have been expected in A's circumstances to take any such step`)) "A could have been expected in A's circumstances to take the steps (section 304C(3))"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits the offence of causing or allowing death in the same household within section 304C(1)` f) "the elements of section 304C(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 304C(4) (src:6953-6959)
@export Frame a charge under section 304C(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing or allowing death of child, domestic worker or vulnerable person in same household), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Household Death Facts` @desc B, the household, the unlawful act, the risk, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 304C(4)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "304C(4)" "causing or allowing death of child below 14 years of age, domestic worker or vulnerable person in same household"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 304C(4)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 304C(4)` f)
        (CONCAT "being a member of the same household as ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " and having frequent contact with the said person, ",
                (IF f's `A was the person whose act caused B's death` THEN "did by your own unlawful act cause the death of the said person, " ELSE "did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take to protect the said person from a significant risk of grievous hurt, whereby the said person died as a result of the unlawful act of a member of the same household, "),
                "to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of causing or allowing death in the same household not made out` f)


§§ `s 308A - causing death in furtherance of group's object`

-- src:7105 | Causing death in furtherance of group’s object
-- src:7107 | 308A.—(1) Any person shall be guilty of an offence who is or acts as a member of a
-- src:7108 | group —
-- src:7110 | (a) knowing that the common object of the members of the group is to commit
-- src:7111 | an offence under this Code or any written law;
-- src:7113 | (b) knowing that —
-- src:7114 | (i) death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the
-- src:7115 | group’s common object; or
-- src:7117 | (ii) a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of
-- src:7118 | offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner
-- src:7119 | against another person in the furtherance of that common object;
-- src:7122 | and
-- src:7124 | (c) the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group’s common
-- src:7125 | object.
-- src:7127 | Illustration
-- src:7129 | Three members of a group including A decide to rob a neighbourhood shop. The
-- src:7130 | group leader, B brings a sharp knife but B reassures A that the knife is only to be used
-- src:7131 | to threaten the shopkeeper, C, and not to harm C. A believes B and takes part in the
-- src:7132 | robbery. C however refuses to surrender his cash to the group. B then stabs C with the
-- src:7133 | knife and C dies from his stab wounds. A is guilty of an offence under this section
-- src:7134 | because A knew that the knife was to be used to threaten another person, C, in
-- src:7135 | furtherance of the group’s common object to commit robbery.
-- src:7139 | (2) A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) shall be punished with
-- src:7140 | imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and
-- src:7141 | shall also be liable to caning.
-- src:7145 | (3) In subsection (1), “group” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Organised
-- src:7146 | Crime Act 2015.
-- "group" is OCA 2015 s 2(1) (s 308A(3)); that Act is not in the sources, so whether
-- there is a group is the first input (FORK DEF-A6).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 308A (src:7105-7146)
DECLARE `Group Object Death Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person whose death was caused, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What was done, and by whom, in furtherance of the group's common object, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "B stabbed the said C with a knife in the course of a robbery"
    `the accused is or acts as a member of a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused, or does the accused act as, a member of a "group"? "Group" has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Organised Crime Act 2015 (s 308A(3)); that Act is not in the sources, so this is for the investigator to answer
    `the accused knows that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused know that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law? (s 308A(1)(a))
    `the accused knows that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused know that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object? (s 308A(1)(b)(i))
    `the accused knows that a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner against another person in the furtherance of that common object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused know that a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner against another person in the furtherance of that common object? Using a knife to threaten counts: "in any manner" (s 308A(1)(b)(ii) and the Illustration)
    `the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the death of a person caused in furtherance of the group's common object? By whom does not matter: the accused need not be the person who caused it (s 308A(1)(c) and the Illustration)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 308A(1) (src:7107-7125)
@export Whether the accused is "guilty of an offence" under section 308A(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (a member of a group who knows of its object and the risk, when a death is caused in furtherance of that object)
GIVEN f IS A `Group Object Death Facts` @desc The group, what the accused knew, and the death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of causing death in furtherance of a group's object within section 308A(1)` f IF
        "Any person shall be guilty of an offence who is or acts as a member of a group"
   ...  f's `the accused is or acts as a member of a group`
   ...  "(a) knowing that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law"
   ...  f's `the accused knows that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law`
   ...  "(b) knowing that"
   ...  (    (    "(i) death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object"
             ...  f's `the accused knows that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object`  )
        OR   (    "(ii) a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner against another person in the furtherance of that common object"
             ...  f's `the accused knows that a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner against another person in the furtherance of that common object` ) )
   ...  "(c) the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object"
   ...  f's `the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 308A(2) (src:7139-7141)
`punishment prescribed by s 308A(2)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "308A(2)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 240
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `not prescribed`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 308A(2) (src:7139-7141)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 308A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing death in furtherance of a group's object)
GIVEN f IS A `Group Object Death Facts` @desc The group, what the accused knew, and the death
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 308A(2)` f IF
        "A person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)"
   ...  `commits the offence of causing death in furtherance of a group's object within section 308A(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Group Object Death Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of causing death in furtherance of a group's object not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is or acts as a member of a group`) "the accused is or acts as a member of a group"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused knows that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law`) "the accused knows that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused knows that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object` OR f's `the accused knows that a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, is to be used in any manner against another person in the furtherance of that common object`) "the accused knows that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object, or that a deadly weapon or anything likely to cause death as a weapon is to be used against another person in furtherance of it"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object`) "the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group's common object"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits the offence of causing death in furtherance of a group's object within section 308A(1)` f) "the elements of section 308A(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 308A(2) (src:7139-7141)
@export Frame a charge under section 308A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing death in furtherance of a group's object), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Group Object Death Facts` @desc The group, what the accused knew, the death, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 308A(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "308A(2)" "causing death in furtherance of a group's object"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 308A(2)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 308A(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "being or acting as a member of a group, knowing that the common object of the members of the group was to commit an offence, and knowing that ",
                (IF f's `the accused knows that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group's common object` THEN "death or grievous hurt was likely to be caused in furtherance of that common object" ELSE "a deadly weapon, or anything which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death, was to be used against another person in the furtherance of that common object"),
                ", did, the death of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                " having been caused in furtherance of that common object, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of causing death in furtherance of a group's object not made out` f)


§§ `s 314 - death caused by act done with intent to cause miscarriage`

-- src:7231 | Death caused by act done with intent to cause miscarriage
-- src:7233 | 314. Subject to the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974, whoever
-- src:7234 | with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child does any act which causes the
-- src:7235 | death of such woman, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend
-- src:7236 | to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine; and if the act is done without the consent of
-- src:7237 | the woman, shall be punished either with imprisonment for life, or with the punishment
-- src:7238 | above-mentioned.
-- src:7240 | Explanation.— It is not essential to this offence that the offender should know that the act is likely to
-- src:7241 | cause death.
-- The Explanation says the offender's knowledge that the act is likely to cause death
-- is not essential; the record carries that knowledge as a leaf the ladder ignores,
-- so the Explanation is a test on both sides (FORK DEF-A7).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 314 (src:7231-7241)
DECLARE `Miscarriage Death Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the woman who died, as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes her, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by administering to the said woman a noxious drug"
    `the woman is with child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the woman with child when the act was done?
    `the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman?
    `the act causes the death of the woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that act cause the death of the woman?
    `not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it NOT an act the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974 authorises? That Act is not encoded; the investigator answers it. (The section is "subject to" that Act.)
    `the act is done without the consent of the woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done without the woman's consent? It does not decide whether the offence is made out; it decides which punishment s 314 states
    `the offender knows that the act is likely to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused know that the act is likely to cause death? NOT an element: the Explanation to s 314 says it "is not essential to this offence", so the answer changes nothing

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 314 (src:7233-7238)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 314 of the Penal Code 1871 (an act done with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child, which causes her death)
GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Death Facts` @desc The woman, the act, and its effect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 314` f IF
        "Subject to the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974,"
   ...  f's `not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`
   ...  "whoever with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child does any act"
   ...  f's `the woman is with child`
   ...  f's `the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman`
   ...  "which causes the death of such woman"
   ...  f's `the act causes the death of the woman`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 314 (src:7233-7238)
`punishment prescribed by s 314` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "314"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 314, without consent (src:7233-7238)
`punishment prescribed by s 314, without consent` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "314, without consent"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for life, or with the punishment above-mentioned"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `or with`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Death Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of causing death by an act done with intent to cause miscarriage not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`) "not authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the woman is with child`) "the woman is with child"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman`) "the accused does an act with intent to cause the miscarriage of the woman"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the act causes the death of the woman`) "the act causes the death of the woman"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 314` f) "the elements of section 314 taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 314 (src:7233-7238)
@export Frame a charge under section 314 of the Penal Code 1871 (death caused by act done with intent to cause miscarriage), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Miscarriage Death Facts` @desc The woman, the act, whether she consented, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 314` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "314" "death caused by act done with intent to cause miscarriage"
        (IF f's `the act is done without the consent of the woman`
         THEN `punishment prescribed by s 314, without consent`'s words
         ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 314`'s words)
        (`offence under s 314` f)
        (CONCAT "with intent to cause the miscarriage of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                ", a woman with child, did an act which caused her death, ",
                (IF f's `the act is done without the consent of the woman` THEN "the act being done without her consent, " ELSE ""),
                "to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of causing death by an act done with intent to cause miscarriage not made out` f)


§§ `s 315 - child destruction before, at or immediately after birth`

-- src:7243 | Child destruction before, at or immediately after birth
-- src:7245 | 315.—(1) Subject to the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974,
-- src:7246 | whoever, with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive, by any
-- src:7247 | intentional act causes a child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother
-- src:7248 | or by such act causes the child to die after its birth, shall, unless such act is immediately
-- src:7249 | necessary to save the life of the mother, be punished with imprisonment for a term not
-- src:7250 | exceeding 10 years, or with fine, or with both.
-- src:7254 | (2) For the purposes of this section, evidence that a woman had at any material time
-- src:7255 | been pregnant for a period of 28 weeks or more shall be prima facie evidence that she
-- src:7256 | was at that time pregnant of a child capable of being born alive.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315 (src:7243-7256)
DECLARE `Child Destruction Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the child, or a description such as "a female child capable of being born alive", as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes the child, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by compressing the head of the child"
    `the accused intends to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the accused intend to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive? Where the woman had been pregnant for 28 weeks or more, s 315(2) makes that prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of such a child: see `s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy`
    `by an intentional act causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, by an intentional act, cause the child to die before it had an existence independent of its mother?
    `by such act causes the child to die after its birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused, by such act, cause the child to die after its birth?
    `the act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act immediately necessary to save the life of the mother? If so, the accused is outside the section
    `not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it NOT an act the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974 authorises? That Act is not encoded; the investigator answers it. (The section is "subject to" that Act.)

DECLARE `Effect of the evidence of the length of a pregnancy` IS ONE OF
    `prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive`
    `not covered by s 315(2)`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315(2) (src:7254-7256)
@export Whether a period of pregnancy is "28 weeks or more" (s 315(2) of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks the woman had been pregnant at the material time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `28 weeks or more` weeks IF weeks AT LEAST 28

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315(2) (src:7254-7256)
@export What evidence of the length of a woman's pregnancy proves under section 315(2) of the Penal Code 1871: at 28 weeks or more, prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive; below that, the subsection says nothing
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks the woman had been pregnant at the material time
GIVETH A `Effect of the evidence of the length of a pregnancy`
`s 315(2) the effect of evidence of the length of the pregnancy` MEANS
    IF `28 weeks or more` weeks
    THEN `prima facie evidence that she was pregnant of a child capable of being born alive`
    ELSE `not covered by s 315(2)`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says what a period of 28 weeks or more is evidence of; it does not say that a shorter pregnancy is evidence the child was not capable of being born alive

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315(1) (src:7245-7250)
@export Whether the accused commits the offence in section 315(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (child destruction before, at or immediately after birth)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Destruction Facts` @desc The accused's intent, the act and the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of child destruction within section 315(1)` f IF
        "Subject to the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974,"
   ...  f's `not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`
   ...  "whoever, with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive,"
   ...  f's `the accused intends to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive`
   ...  "by any intentional act causes a child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother or by such act causes the child to die after its birth"
   ...  (    f's `by an intentional act causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother`
        OR   f's `by such act causes the child to die after its birth` )
   ...  "unless such act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother"
   ...  NOT (f's `the act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless such act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother"

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315(1) (src:7245-7250)
`punishment prescribed by s 315(1)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "315(1)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315(1) (src:7245-7250)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 315(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (child destruction)
GIVEN f IS A `Child Destruction Facts` @desc The accused's intent, the act and the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 315(1)` f IF
        "shall ... be punished with imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years, or with fine, or with both"
   ...  `commits the offence of child destruction within section 315(1)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Child Destruction Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of child destruction not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `not an act authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`) "not authorised by the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused intends to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive`) "the accused intends to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `by an intentional act causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother` OR f's `by such act causes the child to die after its birth`) "by an intentional act the accused causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother, or after its birth"),
        (`missing unless` (NOT (f's `the act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother`)) "the act is not immediately necessary to save the life of the mother"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits the offence of child destruction within section 315(1)` f) "the elements of section 315(1) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 315(1) (src:7245-7250)
@export Frame a charge under section 315(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (child destruction before, at or immediately after birth), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Child Destruction Facts` @desc The accused's intent, the act, the child, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 315(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "315(1)" "child destruction before, at or immediately after birth"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 315(1)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 315(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive, did by an intentional act cause ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                (IF f's `by an intentional act causes the child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother` THEN " to die before it had an existence independent of its mother" ELSE " to die after its birth"),
                ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of child destruction not made out` f)


§§ `s 316 - causing death of a quick unborn child by an act amounting to culpable homicide`

-- src:7258 | Causing death of a quick unborn child by an act amounting to culpable homicide
-- src:7260 | 316. Whoever does any act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death
-- src:7261 | he would be guilty of culpable homicide, and does by such act cause the death of a quick
-- src:7262 | unborn child, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- src:7263 | 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine.
-- src:7265 | Illustration
-- src:7267 | A, knowing that he is likely to cause the death of a pregnant woman, does an act which, if it caused
-- src:7268 | the death of the woman, would amount to culpable homicide. The woman is injured, but does not die;
-- src:7269 | but the death of an unborn quick child with which she is pregnant is thereby caused. A is guilty of the
-- src:7270 | offence defined in this section.
-- "quick unborn child" is not defined in the Code, so it is one input (FORK DEF-A8).
-- The act that "if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide"
-- is a hypothetical about the same act: the caller sets the first leaf from
-- `commits culpable homicide` (pc-body-a-life.l4) on the facts of that act with
-- `causes death by doing an act` set TRUE.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 316 (src:7258-7270)
DECLARE `Quick Unborn Child Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc A description of the unborn child, as it is to appear in the charge - for example "the quick unborn child of C"
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes it, after the description; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by striking the said C in the abdomen with an iron bar"
    `the accused does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act one that, had it caused a person's death, would have made the accused guilty of culpable homicide (s 299)? Set it from `commits culpable homicide` on the facts of the same act with `causes death by doing an act` set TRUE
    `the accused by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause the death of a quick unborn child? The Code does not define "quick": the court's judgement

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 316 (src:7260-7263)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 316 of the Penal Code 1871 (causing death of a quick unborn child by an act amounting to culpable homicide)
GIVEN f IS A `Quick Unborn Child Facts` @desc The act and the unborn child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 316` f IF
        "Whoever does any act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide"
   ...  f's `the accused does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide`
   ...  "and does by such act cause the death of a quick unborn child"
   ...  f's `the accused by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 316 (src:7260-7263)
`punishment prescribed by s 316` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "316"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE


GIVEN f IS A `Quick Unborn Child Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of causing death of a quick unborn child not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide`) "the act is one that, had it caused a person's death, would make the accused guilty of culpable homicide"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the accused by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child`) "by such act the accused causes the death of a quick unborn child"),
        (`missing unless` (`offence under s 316` f) "the elements of section 316 taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 316 (src:7260-7263)
@export Frame a charge under section 316 of the Penal Code 1871 (causing death of a quick unborn child by an act amounting to culpable homicide), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Quick Unborn Child Facts` @desc The act, the unborn child, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 316` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "316" "causing death of a quick unborn child by an act amounting to culpable homicide"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 316`'s words)
        (`offence under s 316` f)
        (CONCAT "did an act under such circumstances that if you had thereby caused death you would have been guilty of culpable homicide, and did by such act cause the death of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                ", a quick unborn child, to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of causing death of a quick unborn child not made out` f)


§§ `s 335A - allowing neglect, physical or sexual abuse of domestic worker or vulnerable person`

-- src:7525 | Allowing neglect, physical or sexual abuse of domestic worker or vulnerable person
-- src:7527 | 335A.—(1) A person (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:7529 | (a) a domestic worker (B) suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or
-- src:7530 | any injury to B’s mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another
-- src:7531 | person (C);
-- src:7533 | (b) A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt,
-- src:7534 | grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C;
-- src:7536 | (c) A was at the time of the risk mentioned in paragraph (b) the employer of B,
-- src:7537 | a member of B’s employer’s household or an employment agent of B;
-- src:7539 | (d) A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to
-- src:7540 | take in A’s circumstances to protect B from the risk mentioned in
-- src:7541 | paragraph (b); and
-- src:7543 | (e) the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to
-- src:7544 | have foreseen.
-- src:7548 | (2) A person (A) shall be guilty of an offence if —
-- src:7551 | (a) a vulnerable person (B) suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or
-- src:7552 | any injury to B’s mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another
-- src:7553 | person (C);
-- src:7555 | (b) A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of neglect, hurt,
-- src:7556 | grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C;
-- src:7558 | (c) A had, at the time of the risk mentioned in paragraph (b), the custody,
-- src:7559 | charge or care of B;
-- src:7561 | (d) A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to
-- src:7562 | take in A’s circumstances to protect B from the risk mentioned in
-- src:7563 | paragraph (b); and
-- src:7565 | (e) the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to
-- src:7566 | have foreseen.
-- src:7570 | (3) For the purposes of this section, “unlawful act”, other than an act by A, is one that
-- src:7571 | constitutes an offence that causes neglect, hurt, grievous hurt or sexual abuse to B or
-- src:7572 | injury to B’s mental health or would constitute such an offence but for being the act
-- src:7573 | of —
-- src:7575 | (a) a person below the age specified in section 82;
-- src:7577 | (b) a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained sufficient
-- src:7578 | maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of the
-- src:7579 | act;
-- src:7581 | (c) a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind;
-- src:7583 | (d) a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication; or
-- src:7585 | (e) a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact.
-- src:7589 | (4) A’s circumstances mentioned in subsections (1)(d) and (2)(d), include but is not
-- src:7590 | limited to A’s past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual
-- src:7591 | abuse or any injury to A’s mental health as a result of an unlawful act by C.
-- src:7595 | (5) Any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall on
-- src:7596 | conviction —
-- src:7598 | (a) in the case where death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable
-- src:7599 | person, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to
-- src:7600 | 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $20,000, or with both; and
-- src:7603 | (b) in any other case, be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
-- src:7604 | extend to 4 years, or with fine which may extend to $4,000, or with both.
-- src:7608 | (6) In this section —
-- src:7610 | “domestic worker”, “employer”, “employment agent” and “member of the
-- src:7611 | employer’s household” have the meanings given by section 73(4);
-- src:7613 | “neglect” has the meaning given by section 304B(2);
-- src:7615 | “sexual abuse” means abuse caused to a victim by the commission of a sexual
-- src:7616 | offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:7617 | Code 2010;
-- src:7619 | “vulnerable person” has the meaning given by section 74A(5).
-- "domestic worker", "employer", "employment agent" and "member of the employer's
-- household" are s 73(4); "vulnerable person" is s 74A(5); "neglect" is s 304B(2);
-- "sexual abuse" is CPC s 2(1) (s 335A(6)).  The first two are the general-part
-- group's, the last is not in the sources, so each is a leaf the investigator answers.
-- Subsection (5)'s death is not an element: it chooses the punishment.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A (src:7525-7619)
DECLARE `Allowing Neglect Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the domestic worker or vulnerable person (B), as it is to appear in the charge
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes B, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused knew and did not do, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by failing to report that the said B's employer's son was repeatedly striking B"
    `B is a domestic worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B a "domestic worker" as section 73(4) gives the meaning (s 335A(6))? See `domestic worker within section 73` in pc-general-part.l4
    `B is a vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is B a "vulnerable person" as section 74A(5) gives the meaning (s 335A(6))? See `vulnerable person within section 74A` in pc-general-part.l4
    `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does B suffer neglect (`s 304B(2) the failure is neglect`), hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse (abuse caused by a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010) or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)? An act is "unlawful" as `s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` says (s 335A(1)(a), (2)(a))
    `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused (A) know, or have reason to believe, that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C? (s 335A(1)(b), (2)(b))
    `A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was A, at the time of the risk, the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B, as section 73(4) gives those meanings? (s 335A(1)(c), for a domestic worker)
    `A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A, at the time of the risk, have the custody, charge or care of B? (s 335A(2)(c), for a vulnerable person)
    `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did A fail to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk? A's circumstances are read with `s 335A(4) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` (s 335A(1)(d), (2)(d))
    `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act occur in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen? (s 335A(1)(e), (2)(e))
    `death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was death caused to B? NOT an element: it chooses which punishment s 335A(5) states, 7 years or fine up to $20,000 or both in that case, otherwise 4 years or fine up to $4,000 or both

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(3) (src:7570-7585)
@export Whether an act other than an act by the accused is "unlawful" within section 335A(3) of the Penal Code 1871: an offence causing neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health, or one that would be but for the actor's age, immaturity, unsoundness of mind, intoxication or mistake of fact
GIVEN u IS A `Unlawful Act Facts` @desc The act, and whether it is an offence or would be but for the actor's excuse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335A(3) the act is unlawful` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF u's `the act is an act of A`
        THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the definition covers an "unlawful" act "other than an act by A"; what makes A's own act unlawful the section does not say
        IF u's `the act constitutes an offence`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person below the age specified in section 82`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person of the age specified in section 83 who had not attained sufficient maturity of understanding to judge of the nature and consequence of the act`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of unsoundness of mind`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of intoxication`
            OR u's `the act would constitute an offence but for being the act of a person entitled to rely on a defence of mistake of fact`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"unlawful act\", other than an act by A, is one that constitutes an offence ... or would constitute such an offence but for being the act of ..." (FORK DEF-A5: a definition read as closed)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(4) (src:7589-7591)
@export Whether an experience is among "A's circumstances" under section 335A(4) of the Penal Code 1871 (A's past or present suffering of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health through an unlawful act by C)
GIVEN `A has past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to A's mental health as a result of an unlawful act by C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does A have such experiences?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335A(4) the circumstance is among A's circumstances` MEANS
    IF `A has past or present experiences of suffering neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to A's mental health as a result of an unlawful act by C`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): A's circumstances "include but is not limited to" those experiences, so any other circumstance may count

-- The other entries of s 335A(6) borrow a meaning from the Code itself: "domestic worker", "employer", "employment agent" and "member of the employer's household" from
-- section 73(4) (`domestic worker within section 73` and the rest in pc-general-part.l4), "neglect" from section 304B(2) (`s 304B(2) the failure is neglect` above) and
-- "vulnerable person" from section 74A(5) (`vulnerable person within section 74A` in pc-general-part.l4); nothing is copied.  "Sexual abuse" is the one entry that
-- means something of its own, by a sexual offence within the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, which is not in the sources: that fact is an input.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(6) (src:7615-7617)
@export Whether abuse is "sexual abuse" under section 335A(6) of the Penal Code 1871: abuse caused to a victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010; abuse that is not so caused is not
GIVEN `the abuse was caused to the victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the abuse caused to the victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010? That Act is not in the sources: the investigator answers it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 335A(6) the abuse is sexual abuse` MEANS
    IF `the abuse was caused to the victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "\"sexual abuse\" means abuse caused to a victim by the commission of a sexual offence within the meaning of section 2(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010" (a "means" definition)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(1) (src:7527-7544)
@export Whether the accused is "guilty of an offence" under section 335A(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (allowing neglect, hurt or abuse of a domestic worker)
GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts` @desc B, the risk, and what A knew, was and did not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker within section 335A(1)` f IF
        "(a) a domestic worker (B) suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)"
   ...  f's `B is a domestic worker`
   ...  f's `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)`
   ...  "(b) A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C"
   ...  f's `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C`
   ...  "(c) A was at the time of the risk mentioned in paragraph (b) the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B"
   ...  f's `A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B`
   ...  "(d) A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk mentioned in paragraph (b)"
   ...  f's `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk`
   ...  "(e) the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen"
   ...  f's `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(2) (src:7548-7566)
@export Whether the accused is "guilty of an offence" under section 335A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (allowing neglect, hurt or abuse of a vulnerable person)
GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts` @desc B, the risk, and what A knew, was and did not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of allowing neglect or abuse of a vulnerable person within section 335A(2)` f IF
        "(a) a vulnerable person (B) suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)"
   ...  f's `B is a vulnerable person`
   ...  f's `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)`
   ...  "(b) A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C"
   ...  f's `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C`
   ...  "(c) A had, at the time of the risk mentioned in paragraph (b), the custody, charge or care of B"
   ...  f's `A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B`
   ...  "(d) A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk mentioned in paragraph (b)"
   ...  f's `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk`
   ...  "(e) the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen"
   ...  f's `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen`

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(5)(a) (src:7598-7600)
`punishment prescribed by s 335A(5)(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "335A(5)(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine which may extend to $20,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 20000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(5)(b) (src:7603-7604)
`punishment prescribed by s 335A(5)(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "335A(5)(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine which may extend to $4,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 48
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 4000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE


@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(5) (src:7595-7604)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 335A(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker)
GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts` @desc B, the risk, and what A knew, was and did not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 335A(1)` f IF
        "Any person who is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) ..."
   ...  `commits the offence of allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker within section 335A(1)` f

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(5) (src:7595-7604)
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 335A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (allowing neglect or abuse of a vulnerable person)
GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts` @desc B, the risk, and what A knew, was and did not do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 335A(2)` f IF
        "Any person who is guilty of an offence under ... subsection (2)"
   ...  `commits the offence of allowing neglect or abuse of a vulnerable person within section 335A(2)` f

GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is a domestic worker`) "B is a domestic worker"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)`) "B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C`) "A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B`) "A was at the time of the risk the employer of B, a member of B's employer's household or an employment agent of B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk`) "A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen`) "the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits the offence of allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker within section 335A(1)` f) "the elements of section 335A(1) taken together"))

GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of allowing neglect or abuse of a vulnerable person not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `B is a vulnerable person`) "B is a vulnerable person"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or any injury to B's mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)`) "B suffers neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person (C)"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of such neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C`) "A knew or had reason to believe that B was at risk of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury caused by C"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B`) "A had, at the time of the risk, the custody, charge or care of B"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk`) "A failed to take such steps as A could reasonably have been expected to take in A's circumstances to protect B from the risk"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen`) "the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that A foresaw or ought to have foreseen"),
        (`missing unless` (`commits the offence of allowing neglect or abuse of a vulnerable person within section 335A(2)` f) "the elements of section 335A(2) taken together"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(5) (src:7595-7604)
@export Frame a charge under section 335A(1) of the Penal Code 1871 (allowing neglect, hurt or abuse of a domestic worker), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts` @desc B, the risk, what A knew and did not do, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 335A(1)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "335A(1)" "allowing neglect, physical or sexual abuse of a domestic worker"
        (IF f's `death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable person`
         THEN `punishment prescribed by s 335A(5)(a)`'s words
         ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 335A(5)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 335A(1)` f)
        (CONCAT "being the employer of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                ", a domestic worker, a member of the employer's household or an employment agent of the said domestic worker, knowing or having reason to believe that the said domestic worker was at risk of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health caused by another person, did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take in your circumstances to protect the said domestic worker from that risk, whereby the said domestic worker suffered such harm as a result of the unlawful act of that person, in circumstances of the kind that you foresaw or ought to have foreseen, to wit, ",
                f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker not made out` f)

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335A(5) (src:7595-7604)
@export Frame a charge under section 335A(2) of the Penal Code 1871 (allowing neglect, hurt or abuse of a vulnerable person), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Allowing Neglect Facts` @desc B, the risk, what A knew and did not do, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 335A(2)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "335A(2)" "allowing neglect, physical or sexual abuse of a vulnerable person"
        (IF f's `death is caused to the domestic worker or vulnerable person`
         THEN `punishment prescribed by s 335A(5)(a)`'s words
         ELSE `punishment prescribed by s 335A(5)(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 335A(2)` f)
        (CONCAT "having the custody, charge or care of ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                ", a vulnerable person, knowing or having reason to believe that the said vulnerable person was at risk of neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or injury to mental health caused by another person, did fail to take such steps as you could reasonably have been expected to take in your circumstances to protect the said vulnerable person from that risk, whereby the said vulnerable person suffered such harm as a result of the unlawful act of that person, in circumstances of the kind that you foresaw or ought to have foreseen, to wit, ",
                f's `the manner`)
        (`elements of allowing neglect or abuse of a vulnerable person not made out` f)
